      },
      "items": [
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "已知卫星",
            "en": "Known Moons"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "木卫一本身是木星的卫星，无天然卫星",
            "en": "Io itself is a moon of Jupiter, has no natural moons"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "卫星名称",
            "en": "Moon Names"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "无",
            "en": "None"
          }
        }
      ],
      "note": {
        "zh": "※ 木卫一是木星四颗伽利略卫星中最内侧的一颗，也是太阳系中密度最大的卫星之一。",
        "en": "※ Io is the innermost of Jupiter's four Galilean moons and one of the densest moons in the Solar System."
      }
    },
    {
      "title": {
        "zh": "🌋 地表特征",
        "en": "🌋 Surface Features"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "主要地形",
            "en": "Main Terrain"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "火山平原、熔岩流、硫磺沉积、火山口、山脉",
            "en": "Volcanic plains, lava flows, sulfur deposits, calderas, mountains"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "最大撞击坑",
            "en": "Largest Crater"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "Tvashtar Paterae（火山口群，直径约 290 公里）",
            "en": "Tvashtar Paterae (volcanic crater complex, ~290 km diameter)"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "地表年龄",
            "en": "Surface Age"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "极年轻，平均约 100 万年（因火山活动不断更新）",
            "en": "Extremely young, average ~1 million years (constantly resurfaced by volcanism)"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "最高峰",
            "en": "Highest Peak"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "Boösaule Montes，约 17,500 米（比珠穆朗玛峰还高）",
            "en": "Boösaule Montes, ~17,500 m (taller than Mount Everest)"
          }
        }
      ],
      "note": {
        "zh": "※ 木卫一表面几乎没有撞击坑，因为火山活动不断覆盖旧地表，使其成为太阳系中地质最年轻的天体之一。",
        "en": "※ Io's surface has almost no impact craters because volcanic activity constantly buries old terrain, making it one of the geologically youngest bodies in the Solar System."
      }
    },
